#
# ENGINE_PIN — the vouchfx engine version and commit this MCP server is pinned to.
#
# What it pins
# ------------
# The first line is  <version> <full-40-character-commit-sha>  — two
# space-separated fields, e.g. "v1.0.0-alpha.9 8c579ab4315cacba4066bc3f33dc24a19ca6c3d1".
# src/Vouchfx.Mcp/EnginePin.cs parses exactly this format.
#
# Unlike vouchfx-samples (which shallow-fetches and builds the engine from
# source at a pinned commit), vouchfx-mcp wraps the PUBLISHED `vouchfx` dotnet
# tool as a subprocess — it never builds the engine from source. The two
# fields therefore pin two different things:
#
#   - VERSION  is what the CLI handshake verifies against at run time: the MCP
#     server invokes the installed `vouchfx` tool, reads its reported version,
#     and refuses to proceed (or warns) if it does not match this line. This
#     is the field that actually gates behaviour.
#
#   - COMMIT SHA is the engine ref that the vendored artefacts this repo ships
#     — the JSON Schema, the generated language reference, and the recipe
#     library (vendored under vendored/ and drift-gated in CI) — are drift-gated against. CI
#     re-generates or diffs those artefacts against the engine source at this
#     exact commit so a silent drift between "what the docs/schema say" and
#     "what the pinned CLI version actually does" is caught mechanically
#     rather than discovered by a user.
#
# A full SHA is required, not a short SHA or a branch/tag name, for the same
# reproducibility reason as every other fleet satellite's ENGINE_PIN: a moving
# ref defeats the point of a pin.
#
# If the SHA above is ever the all-zeros placeholder, EnginePin.Load/Parse
# will refuse to run against it (see EnginePinTests.cs).
#
# When to advance it
# -------------------
# Bump this file when:
#   - a new `vouchfx` pre-release/release is published on NuGet.org that this
#     MCP server should target (most common reason — this repo tracks
#     published tool versions, not engine milestones directly);
#   - the vendored JSON Schema / language reference / recipes need to move to
#     a newer engine commit (e.g. a schema field or step family was added);
#   - the engine's v1.x SDK/event contract freeze advances and this server's
#     event-stream parsing should validate against the new baseline.
#
# How to advance it
# ------------------
# Two easy ways to find the commit SHA for a given tag/release WITHOUT cloning:
#   - GitHub: open the release/tag page (e.g.
#     github.com/tomas-rampas/vouchfx/releases/tag/v1.0.0-alpha.9) and click
#     the short-SHA link under the tag name to reach the full SHA.
#   - `git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/tomas-rampas/vouchfx <tag>`
#     — GOTCHA: vouchfx's tags are ANNOTATED, so this prints TWO lines:
#     `refs/tags/<tag>` (the tag OBJECT's own SHA) and `refs/tags/<tag>^{}`
#     (the COMMIT it points at, "peeled"). Always take the `^{}` line —
#     ENGINE_PIN must hold the commit SHA, never the tag object's SHA.
#     (`gh api repos/tomas-rampas/vouchfx/commits/<tag> --jq .sha` sidesteps
#     this entirely by resolving straight to the commit.)
#
# Steps:
#   1. Pick the new `vouchfx` version to target and its corresponding engine
#      commit SHA (peeled, per the gotcha above).
#   2. Replace the first line of this file with the new "<version> <sha>" pair.
#   3. Re-validate: re-run the packaged-CLI handshake and the vendored
#      artefact drift check (see vendored/README.md) against the new pin.
#   4. Open a PR with just the pin bump (plus any artefact regeneration the
#      new version requires) so the change is reviewable in isolation.
#
